node_modules/
dist/
.wrangler/
*.local
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.dev.vars
.DS_Store
*.log
# ⚠️ …EXCEPT the deploy record. `*.log` above would swallow it, and this file is
# the shared state two concurrent runs use to avoid deploying over each other —
# see scripts/deploy-guard.mjs. Caught 2026-08-13 only because the commit that
# was supposed to publish it reported "nothing to commit".
!docs/deploys.log
.vscode/
!.vscode/extensions.json

# ⚠️ The Calibre-Web Automated data root — the Calibre library, its metadata.db,
# CWA's config, and the ebook files themselves.
#
# NEVER commit this. It is gigabytes of book files, it is the one directory in
# this repo that grows without bound, and this household has already had a
# repo-size incident (377MB .git) force a hosting migration. CWA owns these
# files; git has no business with them.
#
# Note this is the OPPOSITE of the rule in audiobook_catalog, where site/ and the
# covers are deliberately tracked because the deploy ships them from git. That
# repo publishes its outputs; this one serves from D1 and Workers assets, so
# nothing here needs a file to survive in a commit.
runtime/

# Agent worktrees: throwaway git repos created by Claude Code sessions.
# They were committed by accident on 2026-08-10 as embedded repos (gitlinks),
# which clone as empty directories and confuse every later status.
.claude/worktrees/

# ⚠️ The crowdfunding scan's own output — the default file
# `npm run import:crowdfunding` reads.
#
# Gitignored because it carries pledge amounts and the two BackerKit account
# addresses, which are household financial detail rather than catalog data. The
# *shape* is tracked as `scripts/crowdfunding-example.json` and documented in
# `docs/info/crowdfunding-and-accessories.md`; the scan itself is not.
#
# Note this is unlike `scripts/series-overrides.json` and
# `scripts/openlibrary-ids.json`, which ARE tracked on purpose — those are
# ledgers of research nobody wants to redo, and they hold no money.
scripts/crowdfunding-scan.json
scripts/crowdfunding-scan.*.json

# ⚠️ A BUILD ARTIFACT, not a copy of the universe list.
#
# `scripts/sync-universes.mjs` writes these on every build, test and typecheck,
# from catalog-platform/data/. The ONE source of truth is that repo; nothing
# tracked here may hold a second version of those decisions, because two
# versions is exactly the drift the shared list exists to prevent.
#
# It is materialised rather than imported by relative path because the bundler
# needs a static path and the checkout layout is not guaranteed. The sync script
# fails loudly, naming CATALOG_PLATFORM_DIR, if it cannot find the platform repo.
# See docs/info/universes.md.
packages/universes/generated/

# ⚠️ The deploy coordination lock — see scripts/deploy-guard.mjs. Local by
# design: it is about one machine at one moment. The SHARED record is
# docs/deploys.log, which IS tracked.
.deploy.lock
